a large youth mountain biking community  is forming in southern nevada the nevada  south interscholastic cycling league had  so many kids last season they actually  had to turn some away wow as kate  houston reports the league is now in  desperate need of coaches in order to  keep up with demand we just don't have  enough coaches we don't have enough  teams  i've maxed out now for two years and  we're starting to see other teams  getting close to maxing out too thomas  broder is head coach of the vegas  rattlers in the northwest valley which  is one of seven teams in the league 75  kids wanted to join his team last season  but each is capped at 50. i think  everyone for the last couple years just  wants stuff to do with their kids and  their family get them off those their  phones screen time video games this is a  way to do it and i think that's what the  appeal is and that's what created so  much growth each team is made up of  middle and high school students in their  immediate area the league hopes to bring  on 20 to 30 more coaches to keep up with  the 300 anticipated kids this season we  train people from all levels to first  year riders to veterans who are picking  up some additional skills we can teach  them league director dennis lefler says  a majority of the coaches are parents  that want to share a passion with their  kids once they start they're hooked you  really got these kids that never knew  each other that are now interacting and  the closeness of these teams and the  camaraderie when we're out there at our  events  people become friends and and meet  throughout the year and it's really fun  and exciting to see that happen kate  houston live local now  they are trying to raise about 30  thousand dollars for all the equipment  that they need for this season in order  to register to coach or to donate you  can head to our website at 8newsnow.com
 

